enable-network-defaults-for-workspace

Lane: cross

Unit: enable-network-for-workspace-profiles

ChildPatch: enable-network-defaults-for-workspace

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Enable network access for the built-in Workspace profile and profiles that inherit it, with matching permission descriptions and status.

Requires: none

Provides: Enable the native Workspace preset network policy, carry that default through permission-profile inheritance, preserve explicit network restrictions and read-only defaults, and present the effective network policy consistently in permission choices and live and preview status.

Boundary: Filesystem roots and local directory preparation remain with configure-workspace-roots-from-project-directory. Approval defaults, trust-controlled configuration, managed restrictions, named-profile overrides, Full Access confirmation and keyboard ordering remain with their native or independent owners.

Verification: Protocol preset and Core configuration tests cover unchanged filesystem defaults, enabled Workspace network, inheritance and explicit restrictions. CLI and app-server checks cover selected Workspace network and filesystem enforcement. TUI permission descriptions, status labels and live/setup previews reflect the effective network policy.

CrossGroup: workspace-permissions


